  "retrievedAt": "2026-08-27",
  "readMethod": "Pixel read. Candle grid recovered from the coloured columns (137 bars at 12.6985px); for each column the wide run of colour gave the body's two edges and the one-pixel runs above and below gave the wick's. Green closes higher, which fixes which body edge is the open. Prices come from a least-squares fit of the seventeen LABELLED gridlines on the price axis, 11,600 to 18,400.",
  "accuracy": "+/- 5 IDR, about half a pixel. Fit residuals across the seventeen labels run -4.2 to +4.2; TradingView's own two price tags (last close 16,575 and SMA100 15,623) come back 6 IDR low, inside the same tolerance.",
  "notKnown": "PER-BAR DATES AND VOLUME. A chart image carries neither. The window is read off the month axis and is stated above; individual bars are NOT dated, and nothing in the episode may date one.",
  "clippedLastBar": "TradingView clips a 138th bar against the price axis. It is excluded: a half-drawn candle cannot be read. Its close is the 16,575 tag.",
  "ma100": {
    "what": "The purple SMA 100 the chart draws, read off the line itself rather than computed.",
    "why": "A 100-bar average over a 137-bar window is null for its first 99 bars, so a computed line would begin three-quarters of the way across. TradingView computes it from history before this window, and that history is not in the picture. The line that IS in the picture is the honest source.",
    "interpolated": [
      60,
      61,
      63,
      90,
      112,
      118,
      131
    ],
    "interpolatedNote": "Bars where a candle body covers the line. Filled straight across; an SMA100 moves a few rupiah a day, so the error is under the read's own tolerance."
  },
  "windowNote": "Read off the month axis, not assumed. TradingView labels the first bar of each month; those labels land on bars 17, 37, 55, 72, 93, 109 and 129, and the gaps between them are 20/18/17/21/16/20 bars \u2014 IDX trading days per month. Stepping back one month from the January label at bar 17 puts bars 0-16 in December 2025.",
